  "id": "ar-model",
  "term": "AR model",
  "definition": "An AR model, here meaning a conditional Poisson autoregressive model, is a statistical time-series approach that uses earlier observations to describe how current count data vary over time. In this context, it is used to capture departures from an expected power-law pattern, such as changes in posting activity around social events.",
